#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059465 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cc0e4fc-64ca-5c1b-abbe-357e930af7a4" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Length of the Hypotenuse to the Length Of the Shortest Side"}] :question/id #uuid "b5f19406-37c2-569e-9c9e-b99e00234f91" :question/math-academy-id "e-3084" :question/problem "What is the length of the hypotenuse in a $30^\\circ$-$60^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle if the side opposite the $30^\\circ$ angle has a length of $6\\,\\textrm{cm}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's refer to our standard $30^\\circ$-$60^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle.\n\n![](images/5f/5fe1cd7975f1537bead1f9560816dafe5e8f3ec0db3e683e2bd3e00c4ac54506.png)\n\nIn any $30^\\circ$-$60^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle, the hypotenuse is twice the length of the shorter leg.\n\nThe leg opposite the $30^\\circ$ angle is the shorter leg of the triangle. So here, the shorter leg has length $x=6\\, \\text{cm}.$\n\nSo here, the length of the hypotenuse must be\n\n$$\n2 \\cdot 6 = 12\\,\\textrm{cm}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26db86bd-122c-5d1b-9684-9444897d1c44" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Length of the Shorter Leg to the Length of the Longer Leg"}] :question/id #uuid "f399fe29-f767-5ea5-bc2b-0d47c0e8fbaf" :question/math-academy-id "e-3086" :question/problem "In the triangle below, what is the length of the shorter leg?\n\n![](images/ae/aeb29243195210194a1f114fdf5146bcbd418180c957d5a1c88c3f1055a5c5c9.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's refer to our standard $30^\\circ$-$60^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle.\n\n![](images/58/58993cc083d8561501ea9db70c6d4d886fadc4d4ac3455a1a58de1fe5ceb6e77.png)\n\nSince this is a $30^\\circ$-$60^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle, the length of the longer leg is $\\sqrt{3}$ times that of the shorter leg.\n\nHere, the longer leg has length $2,$ and the shorter leg has length $x,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\sqrt{3}x \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo remove the radical from the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and denominator by the radical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the length of the shorter leg is $\\dfrac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059468 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca6bd1cf-98e8-5fc8-b605-dd4d24ac8f6c" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Length of the Hypotenuse to the Length Of the Longer Leg"}] :question/id #uuid "40a94955-95e0-5945-9a84-d51b8c691bce" :question/math-academy-id "e-3088" :question/problem "What is the length of the longer leg in a $30^\\circ$-$60^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle if the hypotenuse has a length of $6?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's refer to our standard $30^\\circ$-$60^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle.\n\n![](images/9f/9f62659af506661e1343caef0afa5f2072298879f17dcf8a44ab610f51f1e30f.png)\n\nSince the hypotenuse has a length of $6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =6 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know $x,$ we can calculate the length of the longer leg as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}x = \\sqrt{3} \\cdot 3 = 3\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the longer leg has a length of $3 \\sqrt{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cc0e4fc-64ca-5c1b-abbe-357e930af7a4" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Length of the Hypotenuse to the Length Of the Shortest Side"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148fdab1-8b39-57a5-a1eb-257f125259da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490552} {:answer/id #uuid "65b4e9e2-a8b5-557e-b3ab-0b84691b73ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490701} {:answer/id #uuid "e22a80c9-1249-51e0-a0ba-6334f6321b88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490940} {:answer/id #uuid "e663f196-26e3-5865-90cd-f9f7bafae825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490952} {:answer/id #uuid "ee62716b-6528-5274-8112-c28d45fbd1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee62716b-6528-5274-8112-c28d45fbd1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490966} :answer-field/id #uuid "70cd67f9-591e-55a5-b083-9db1d0fe8212" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db5b38a7-1e2b-5723-a09c-8e7764a83012" :question/math-academy-id "q-119478" :question/problem "What is the length of the hypotenuse in a ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle if the side opposite the ${30}^{∘}$ angle has a length of $12?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's refer to our standard ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle.\n\n![](images/ec/ec6541d0566750d1057627a510020c572ff8a856cc5ff5e8d02d0aef0a783683.png)\n\nIn any ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle, the length of the hypotenuse is twice the length of the shorter leg.\n\nThe leg opposite the ${30}^{∘}$ angle is the shorter leg of the triangle. So here, the shorter leg has length $x=12.$\n\nTherefore, the length of the hypotenuse must be\n\n$$\n2\\cdot 12=24.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca6bd1cf-98e8-5fc8-b605-dd4d24ac8f6c" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Length of the Hypotenuse to the Length Of the Longer Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "435f55ff-e092-5ce8-84f6-12055ae4ce9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{40\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490638} {:answer/id #uuid "b07e562a-0853-53ac-a000-1db48b360e7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490862} {:answer/id #uuid "efb7d154-b0e7-5163-bd5a-c4b4101a3669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{80\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490969} {:answer/id #uuid "f44c2ba2-6687-5443-ad13-986c61e2ee78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490979} {:answer/id #uuid "feca5556-b7c0-59fc-92f6-0a0631232337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efb7d154-b0e7-5163-bd5a-c4b4101a3669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{80\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490969} :answer-field/id #uuid "dddfd95a-9c26-5c26-bff5-61ee818e4583" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "509c2568-daff-51e3-8d7b-274974125a51" :question/math-academy-id "q-22563" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d162f5a85434a7798dd29a42bb45dd801d38560f6ad1aeea090c9d371a024dd2.png)\n\nGiven that the triangle $△ABC$ above is an equilateral triangle and $AH=40,$ what is the length of $\\overset{―}{AC}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's draw triangle $△ABH,$ which is a ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle.\n\n![](images/7c/7cbfe29dd9087d07b6d2101e85b9154836704221320f4dd19346f49f3a858fa3.png)\n\n \n\nSince the longer leg, $\\overset{―}{AH},$ has a length of $40,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}x & =40 \\\\ x & =\\frac{40}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now calculate the length of the hypotenuse, $\\overset{―}{AB},$ as follows:\n\n$$\nAB=2x=2\\cdot \\frac{40\\sqrt{3}}{3}=\\frac{80\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $△ABC$ is an equilateral triangle, we get\n\n$$\nAC=AB=\\frac{80\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cc0e4fc-64ca-5c1b-abbe-357e930af7a4" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Length of the Hypotenuse to the Length Of the Shortest Side"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e29552f-3c64-50c3-a1f2-e873ae2dcbc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490538} {:answer/id #uuid "2a630dfd-6a80-5472-8816-e5ea00c29ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490594} {:answer/id #uuid "4ac7f36a-5af8-5783-bb77-840908626639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490654} {:answer/id #uuid "578994ac-61ed-547a-aa46-81a575b954ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490676} {:answer/id #uuid "6e72deb9-362f-5bc3-8d16-f9816c6767c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "578994ac-61ed-547a-aa46-81a575b954ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490676} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b8994a7-f1b4-59c9-967c-c4f5d8ad4f3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "982fa796-ae1b-56f3-a685-bbc7a4be79d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-53452" :question/problem "![](images/e8/e86f0e2fab2e18a2c5c8991292ed9c2bb36d953758b0e5e217d952d9524325ba.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of the hypotenuse of the ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's refer to our standard $30$-$60$-$90$ triangle.\n\n![](images/77/77da0f6ea00a2d1877198387967157f62011356e859ebd2c2cd7cabea074fa85.png)\n\nIn any ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle, the length of the hypotenuse is twice the length of the shorter leg.\n\nThe leg opposite the ${30}^{∘}$ angle is the shorter leg of the triangle. So here, the shorter leg has length $x=6.$\n\nTherefore, the length of the hypotenuse must be\n\n$$\n2\\cdot 6=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26db86bd-122c-5d1b-9684-9444897d1c44" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Length of the Shorter Leg to the Length of the Longer Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a13dd3d7-7d4b-511c-98b3-1fb34b586586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058375} {:answer/id #uuid "ad099d01-153c-5da1-8c13-70001e79259f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058376} {:answer/id #uuid "28172104-fbc6-5edb-abf9-2de83a2f54e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058377} {:answer/id #uuid "50e5b6ea-3ad1-5a85-a909-971d765bf4f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058378} {:answer/id #uuid "78dfb064-626f-5875-83b6-9a0b25999591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50e5b6ea-3ad1-5a85-a909-971d765bf4f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058378} :answer-field/id #uuid "a32854f4-ad0c-55ab-8184-cc97f0f66b55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "696e1f33-11e8-591d-a151-94309c4bb3e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-53472" :question/problem "![](images/9a/9aef509e210c6d64da56119083ba36d9cc1f4e9b4533cf68285806a5606881cb.png)\n\nIn the triangle above, what is the length of $\\overset{―}{AC}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's refer to our standard ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle.\n\n![](images/27/277e019b26f72cffd7647abe694338acd099e4d48fc532a7e9d6ad362a49dcc9.png)\n\nSince this is a ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle, the length of the longer leg is $\\sqrt{3}$ times that of the shorter leg.\n\nHere, the shorter leg has length $x=6$ and the longer leg has length $\\sqrt{3}x,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{AC}=\\sqrt{3}x=\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 6=6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the length of the longer leg is $6\\sqrt{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491122 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059639 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26db86bd-122c-5d1b-9684-9444897d1c44" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Length of the Shorter Leg to the Length of the Longer Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1374d11c-c274-5b91-9dfe-0f7e167fca92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490549} {:answer/id #uuid "35c64c7a-ca3e-5dd3-84ef-710d5a28937f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490613} {:answer/id #uuid "639c1b69-947d-5cd8-8ecb-2f5ef187cc55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490697} {:answer/id #uuid "da7ad1da-7d39-59eb-b693-25c2b70b6956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490925} {:answer/id #uuid "f35c6581-5112-5507-965d-4bcf9a92adf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35c64c7a-ca3e-5dd3-84ef-710d5a28937f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490613} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fc1ce35-b16a-5cf4-8d4b-a342c8635f62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17205a41-6674-51a4-9c40-4ba01f9e707f" :question/math-academy-id "q-82320" :question/problem "![](images/78/7829be694b61852c312f8f12ae9f7f789f445913f7ef043ce53198aacbc7afef.png)\n\nIn the triangle above, what is the length of $\\overset{―}{AC}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's refer to our standard ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle.\n\n![](images/85/85f119cdc6b7a80dd7cd4ea2a2a235e80723b7c2fe6837fa127beb8fd994d7ea.png)\n\nSince this is a ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle, the length of the longer leg is $\\sqrt{3}$ times that of the shorter leg.\n\nHere, the shorter leg has length $x=2\\sqrt{3}$ and the longer leg has length $\\sqrt{3}x,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC=\\sqrt{3}x=\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=3\\cdot 2=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the length of the longer leg is $6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491188 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca6bd1cf-98e8-5fc8-b605-dd4d24ac8f6c" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Length of the Hypotenuse to the Length Of the Longer Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fef6c0c-8eb2-5a73-b836-5681122998f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490603} {:answer/id #uuid "69ee155c-b171-56ea-9d13-8bca83527d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490710} {:answer/id #uuid "92b763ce-2c9b-5ccd-802c-aa8057fcd06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490809} {:answer/id #uuid "d417332f-75ba-5c5b-b8ae-4de6ff711cf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490911} {:answer/id #uuid "f16d4860-92d9-5279-b9a3-994bb21f2941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69ee155c-b171-56ea-9d13-8bca83527d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490710} :answer-field/id #uuid "021f1c31-0686-5d93-8ec9-4f4637fa173e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "afcbfe34-2a53-5e47-b9d2-1086902c80be" :question/math-academy-id "q-82341" :question/problem "What is the length of the longer leg in a ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle if the hypotenuse has a length of $2?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's refer to our standard ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle. \n\n![](images/03/032bc058139e8f2b9381510a1f5817b73632b1015f3bc0a364e227001c383bb8.png)\n\nSince the hypotenuse has a length of $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now calculate the length of the longer leg as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}x=\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1=\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the longer leg has a length of $\\sqrt{3}.$"}]}
